{"name":"Paper Plane","hex":"#f1ece0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"paper plane","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Clipping of paper airplane.","Clipping of paper aeroplane."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paper_plane"}],"entries":[{"title":"Paper plane","blocks":[{"text":"A paper plane is a toy aircraft, usually a glider, made out of a single folded sheet of paper or paperboard. It typically takes the form of a simple nose-heavy triangle thrown like a dart."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Papierflieger_--_2021_--_7215.jpg/330px-Papierflieger_--_2021_--_7215.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paper_plane","wikidata":"Q73767"},{"title":"Paper plane (cocktail)","blocks":[{"text":"The paper plane is a whiskey-based cocktail created in 2008. In 2020 it was added to the International Bartenders Association's (IBA) list of official cocktails as a new era drink."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Taub_Family_Outpost_-_June_11_2021_-_Sarah_Stierch_02.jpg/330px-Taub_Family_Outpost_-_June_11_2021_-_Sarah_Stierch_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paper_plane_(cocktail)","wikidata":"Q96398368"},{"title":"Paper","blocks":[{"text":"Paper is a thin sheet of matted cellulose fibers. Largely derived from lignocellulose, paper is created from a pulp dissolved into a slurry that is drained and dried into sheets. Different types of paper are defined by constituent fiber, paper pulp, sizing, coating, paper size, paper density and grammage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Various_products_made_from_paper.JPG/330px-Various_products_made_from_paper.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paper","wikidata":"Q11472"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Paper_Airplane.png/500px-Paper_Airplane.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Paper_Airplane.png/500px-Paper_Airplane.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Folding instructions for a traditional classic dart","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APaper_Airplane.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/N-424_Paper_Plane.gif/330px-N-424_Paper_Plane.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/N-424_Paper_Plane.gif/330px-N-424_Paper_Plane.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ninomiya's \"N-424\" design from Jet Age Jamboree (1966). The glider fuselage is constructed from several laminations of paper glued together. The wings are of two laminations, and the tailplane and tailfin of a single lamination.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AN-424_Paper_Plane.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Torque_paper_jet.JPG/500px-Torque_paper_jet.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Torque_paper_jet.JPG/500px-Torque_paper_jet.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An example of an asymmetrical custom paper airplane, which exhibits large torque due to unbalanced forces on the wings. The flight path assumes a somewhat parabolic shape, before descending in a rapid counter-clockwise spiral, as viewed from behind.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATorque_paper_jet.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Chinese_hemp_paper_western_han.jpg/500